---
// Real capture, taken on a throwaway profile registering only a fictional
// `checkout-service` repo. The whole window, uncropped and unretouched.
//
// What it actually shows: three agent tabs (Claude, Copilot, Codex) over one
// repository, a live Codex session, a shell running `git status` with its real
// output, the file tree, a rendered README, and the status bar. The agents are
// idle and all sit on `main`, so the caption claims neither work in flight nor
// per-agent branches, and there is deliberately no running/waiting/done/error
// legend. The four states are labelled in the worktree figure further down,
// where a real example backs each one.
//
// Three candidates, sized to what each visitor actually needs. The frame is
// 1100 CSS px on desktop but only ~348 on a phone, where a 1.75x screen needs
// ~610 physical px, so serving 1100w there wasted 23 KB, so 700w covers it.
const width = 1100
const height = 668
---
<section class="shot">
  <div class="shot-frame metal-frame">
    <img
      src="/images/workspace.webp"
      srcset="/images/workspace@700.webp 700w, /images/workspace.webp 1100w, /images/workspace@2x.webp 2200w"
      sizes="(max-width: 1164px) calc(100vw - 64px), 1100px"
      alt="The Manifold workspace: Claude Code, Copilot and Codex agents open as tabs over one repository, with a shell running git status, the file tree and a rendered README"
      width={width}
      height={height}
      loading="eager"
      decoding="async"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />
  </div>
  <p class="shot-caption">Three agents, a shell and the docs. One window, one repository.</p>
</section>

<style>
  .shot { max-width: 1100px; margin: var(--space-2xl) auto 0; padding: 0 var(--space-xl); }
  .shot-frame img { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }

  .shot-caption {
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
  }
</style>
